  "name": "Pulse Width Pocket",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A swung pulse bass: a hollow pulse whose width narrows and widens in a quarter-note-triplet pocket, with a faster square flicker for bounce, like a wobbling hollow tube over a clean sine sub. Play: long and short F1, G1 and A#1 notes at 140-150 BPM with the transport running; the triplet pocket slides against straight eighths and the pulse stays centred and mono. Macros: Pocket Depth swings the notch and pulse width harder, Hollowness sharpens the notch resonance, Flicker adds an eighth-note square jump and Air opens the top end.",
